{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_011Ch3nA2GxwtmM8Vqnox69H","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've fixed the typo, but I haven't committed yet because of the commit message.\n\n**The fix.** `wholsale` appeared once in each of `data/2025-10.csv`, `2025-11.csv` and `2025-12.csv`, and those were the only matches in the repo. I changed all three to `wholesale`. That's one line per file, no `wholsale` is left, and `check.sh` passes. Since all three files are from 2025, this time the check did cover them.\n\n**The commit message.** `CLAUDE.md` says commit messages start with the data month because the import log is grouped by it. This single commit touches three months, so one month prefix would misfile the fix for the other two. I can't see how the import log reads the prefix, so I don't want to guess at a format. Which would you like?\n1. `2025-10..2025-12: fix wholsale → wholesale` (one commit, but the import log may not parse a range).\n2. `2025-12: fix wholsale → wholesale in 2025-10..12` (it parses, but the log files it all under December).\n3. Three commits, one per month. Each prefix stays accurate, but reverting takes three steps. A single `git revert --no-commit` over the range followed by one commit still undoes it in one go.\n\nThe changes are staged in the working tree and ready to go once you pick.","citations":[]}],"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-5.5","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":523,"cache_read_input_tokens":23171,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":523,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":"standard","speed":"standard"},"provider":"Anthropic","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<uuid-1>","uuid":"<uuid-84>","timestamp":"2026-11-15T00:37:47.147Z","request_id":"gen-17947030